    "review_surface": "racer-hd-asset-dossier/review/index.html",
    "disposition": "Fifth sequence-level refinement separates rim/spoke, hub, and crank/pedal hardware depth without changing occupancy, envelope or contact. The wheel assembly reads more mechanically layered, but crank/pedal forms remain schematic at true density. None of the ten unique poses is shipping-ready."
  },
  "family_blockers": [
    {
      "code": "saddle-volume-attachment",
      "description": "The new restrained saddle/post clamp makes attachment readable, but the saddle bodies still read as broad primitive caps with limited underside thickness/profile modeling; refine the seat volume while preserving the stock envelope."
    },
    {
      "code": "frame-junction-modeling",
      "description": "Shared crown collars improve fork/frame continuity and corrected P2 centers align material with geometry, but several intersections still read as simplified members meeting a collar rather than fully integrated high-resolution hardware."
    },
    {
      "code": "hardware-depth-integration",
      "description": "Rim/spoke, hub and drivetrain now use distinct shared depth treatments, substantially reducing the previous flat neutral-hardware read. The remaining blocker is geometric integration of the crank/pedal forms, which still read as simplified bars at true density."
    }
  ],
